{"name":"Ghost Writer","hex":"#bcb7ad","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ghost writer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of ghostwriter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ghost_writer"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Ghost Writer (film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Ghost Writer is a 2010 neo-noir political thriller film directed by Roman Polanski. The film is an adaptation of the 2007 novel, The Ghost, by Robert Harris with the screenplay written by Polanski and Harris. It stars Ewan McGregor in the title role with Pierce Brosnan, Kim Cattrall, and Olivia Williams."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1a/The_Ghost_Writer_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ghost_Writer_(film)","wikidata":"Q157879"},{"title":"Ghost Writer (Hong Kong TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Ghost Writer is a 2010 Hong Kong television series produced by TVB, starring Steven Ma and Linda Chung. The protagonist of the series, Po Chung-ling, is based on the author of Strange Stories from a Chinese Studio, a collection of Chinese tales on the supernatural. The series tells how he was inspired to write those stories based on his personal encounters with the supernatural, as well as her relationship with Lau Sum-Yu."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f5/GhostWriter%28TVB%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_Writer_(Hong_Kong_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q5557226"},{"title":"Ghost Writer (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Ghost Writer is the second solo album by Garland Jeffreys, released by A&M Records in 1977. It was recorded with an all-star lineup of session musicians, including Dr. John, The Brecker Brothers, Anthony Jackson, Steve Gadd, Hugh McCracken, David Spinozza, and Leon Pendarvis. Alongside the tracks specially recorded for the album, it includes Jeffreys' earlier song \"Wild in the Streets\", recorded with Dr. John and his band and released as a single by Atlantic Records in 1973."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c2/Ghost_Writer_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_Writer_(album)","wikidata":"Q5557223"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1a/The_Ghost_Writer_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1a/The_Ghost_Writer_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Ghost_Writer_poster.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/The_Ghostwriter_-_ferry.jpg/500px-The_Ghostwriter_-_ferry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/The_Ghostwriter_-_ferry.jpg/1280px-The_Ghostwriter_-_ferry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/The_Ghostwriter_-_ferry.jpg/500px-The_Ghostwriter_-_ferry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Ghostwriter_-_ferry.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f5/GhostWriter%28TVB%29.jpg/250px-GhostWriter%28TVB%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f5/GhostWriter%28TVB%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f5/GhostWriter%28TVB%29.jpg/250px-GhostWriter%28TVB%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki